<noinclude>
Holds the state of a user's currently-running Start/Stop timer (customer, job, task, start time, timezone). The
TimeTracker extension writes one of these at <code>User:&lt;user&gt;/TimeTracker/running</code> when a timer starts
and reads it back on stop; it is transient state, not a stored time entry, and is not edited by hand.
<code>customer</code> and <code>job</code> are page ids; their names are shown via DisplayTitle. When the timer stops
the page is blanked.
[[Category:Time tracker templates]]
